\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab For the might of Thine arm we bless
\par \pard\li720 Thee, our God, our father's God ;
\par Thou hast kept thy pilgrim people by the 
\par Strength of Thy staff and rod ;
\par Thou hast called us to the journey which 
\par Faithless feet ne'er trod ;
\par For the might of thine arm we bless Thee,
\par Our God, our fathers' God.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab For the love of Christ constraining, the 
\par \pard\fi360\li360 bound their hearts as one ;
\par For the faith in truth and freedom in 
\par which their work was done ;
\par For the peace of God's evangel wherewith
\par their feet were shod ;
\par For the might of Thine arm we bless Thee,
\par our God, our fathers' God.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab We are watchers of a beacon whose light 
\par \pard\li720 Must never die ;
\par We are guardians of an altar that shows
\par Thee ever nigh ;
\par We are children of Thy freemen who sleep
\par Beneath the sod ;
\par For the might of Thine arm we bless Thee,
\par Our God, our father's God.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab May the shadow of Thy presence around
\par \pard\fi360\li360 our camp be spread ;
\par \pard\li720 Baptize us with the courage Thou gavest
\par to our dead ;
\par O keep us in the pathway their saintly
\par feet have trod ;
\par For the might of Thine arm we bless thee,
\par our God, our father's God.
\par \pard 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

